!public/data/sf/sf-footprint-supplement.json
public/data/sf/*.json.gz
# ...except the compact city asset the canonical runtime boots from. It is
# 5 MB, and the native build (eo-data DataPaths) finds the repo root by it and
# will not boot without it -- so a clone needs it tracked. Its
# source URLs, licences, attribution and SHA-256 digests are in meta.sources.
!public/data/sf/sf-city.json.gz
# ...and the real car parks / green areas layer (scripts/build-sf-lots-parks.mjs,
# ODbL, 0.45 MB; attribution in sf-lots-parks.NOTICE.txt beside it). Without it
# a clone or deploy draws no lots and no greens.
!public/data/sf/sf-lots-parks.json.gz
# ...and the world stream's footprint pack (scripts/build-sf-footprint-pack.mjs,
# DataSF Building Footprints, PDDL-1.0, 9.6 MB; provenance in
# sf-footprints.NOTICE.txt beside it). Without it the streamed city past the
# boot window shows only the extract's 28,000 footprints.
!public/data/sf/sf-footprints.json.gz
# ...and the city's street storm drains (scripts/build-sf-storm-drains.mjs,
# DataSF jtgq-b7c5, PDDL, 0.16 MB; see sf-storm-drains.NOTICE.txt). Without it
# the detail pass falls back to its invented corner drains.
!public/data/sf/sf-storm-drains.json.gz
# ...and the citywide map cartography (scripts/map/build-citywide-map.mjs,
# ODbL + PDDL, 3.5 MB; provenance in sf-map-citywide.NOTICE.txt beside it).
# The pause map, the corner map and the GPS read it for every district past the
# boot window; without it they fall back to the loaded district.
!public/data/sf/sf-map-citywide.json.gz
public/data/sf/*.geojson
public/data/sf/*.pbf

